&lt;p&gt;This role is part of our&lt;a href=&quot;https://prerender.io/&quot;&gt; Prerender&lt;/a&gt; team, one of our largest brands at&lt;a href=&quot;http://saas.group/&quot;&gt; saas.group&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prerender is a dynamic rendering SaaS platform within the&lt;a href=&quot;http://saas.group/&quot;&gt; saas.group&lt;/a&gt; portfolio. Since 2017, we&#39;ve revolutionized SEO practices by enabling search engines to crawl JavaScript-heavy sites seamlessly while preserving user experience. Thousands of companies worldwide trust our platform, which serves over 2.7 billion unique pages to web crawlers and drives results for enterprises and growing businesses alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Profile Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prerender has built a platform that thousands of companies trust to serve billions of pages to web crawlers. Now we&#39;re evolving into something bigger: the layer that makes the web legible to machines, both the search crawlers that have always mattered and the AI systems that increasingly decide what people find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To get there, we need to transform how we build product. We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Chief Technology Officer (CTO)&lt;/strong&gt; to lead that transformation, shifting our engineering organization from infrastructure-optimization to a high-velocity, product-focused team that moves fast and ships features that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a building role, not a caretaker role. You&#39;ll own the technology vision, set the engineering strategy, and have authority over the R&amp;amp;D budget, team, and technical direction. You&#39;ll embed AI-first engineering practices, make smart infrastructure tradeoffs, and build the improvement motion that makes delivery faster and keeps it that way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead a small, senior engineering team — around seven engineers today — supported by shared platform and DevOps resources from&lt;a href=&quot;http://saas.group&quot;&gt; saas.group&lt;/a&gt;&#39;s central team. There is no management layer between you and the engineers, which puts you close to the work and means the leadership has to come from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So we need someone hands-on enough to augment the team, not to manage it from a distance, and who can do that without losing hold of the strategy and the responsibilities only this role carries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We need deep technical expertise, a strong infrastructure background, and a proven track record of transforming engineering teams at SaaS companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Vision and Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technology vision, roadmap, and engineering strategy for Prerender. Align engineering work with business objectives and customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead adoption of AI-assisted development tooling to multiply team productivity; own the quality bar for what it produces.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive architecture and infrastructure decisions with a holistic view of TCO that includes maintenance burden and engineering opportunity cost, not just hosting spend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a multi-region, Kubernetes-based render fleet efficiently: cost per render, reliability, and the operational hygiene that keeps both from drifting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Prerender&#39;s technical capabilities to customers, partners, and the broader market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards of software quality, performance, security, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track shifts in technology and engineering practice, and bring the ones that change how we build into the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security and Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own security and compliance as a standing program. Prerender completes SOC 2 Type II and its ISO 27001 certification decision at the end of 2026; you inherit the year-two observation period, the surveillance audit, and the operational discipline that keeps both credible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the program legible to someone other than you: named owners, current vendor and auditor contacts, and no single point of failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Management and Growth:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor engineers to reach their full potential. Set clear expectations and create opportunities for growth. &lt;strong&gt;People matter here.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a culture of ownership, where engineers carry their decisions through instead of escalating them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster diversity and inclusion within the engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution and Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the continuous improvement motion of delivery. The team finds and removes its own bottlenecks on a regular cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance DevOps practices, CI/CD pipelines, and robust monitoring systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track engineering metrics that matter. Use data to identify bottlenecks and optimize workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage change deliberately.&lt;/strong&gt; Changes to practice, process and infrastructure reach the people who have to run them — and, where customers are affected, the customers — with notice, consultation, and a route to raise a question before the change lands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Partnership and Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the CEO and leadership team on company strategy. Communicate technology progress to company leadership and the board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work closely with Product to align engineering capacity with customer needs.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate technical concepts for non-technical stakeholders and advocate for investments that drive business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership &amp;amp; Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full R&amp;amp;D budget including personnel, infrastructure, tooling, and vendor relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run that budget as a managed number.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain an infrastructure cost model, report forecast against actual, and be able to say what a decision costs before it&#39;s made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the right decisions for engineering, aligned with company strategy, without second-guessing or micromanagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You bring to the table&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in software engineering, with 5+ years in senior engineering leadership (VP/Director/CTO) at a SaaS company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong infrastructure background&lt;/strong&gt; with experience running large-scale distributed systems and production Kubernetes, and making strategic tradeoffs between cost, maintenance burden, and engineering velocity. You&#39;ve driven unit costs down on a fleet you owned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated ability to embed AI tooling into engineering workflows and multiply team productivity&lt;/strong&gt;, with a clear-eyed view of where it helps, where it produces plausible work that doesn&#39;t hold up, and how review standards survive the increase in volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience coaching, mentoring, and developing engineering teams, ideally through a significant transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of raising a team&#39;s delivery speed and keeping it raised long after the initial push, with the measurement and process change that made it stick.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of landing process and platform change that sticks, with the people affected brought along before it landed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a security and compliance program in a SaaS company — SOC 2, ISO 27001 or equivalent — as a continuing operational responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-oriented and hands-on: you understand how engineering decisions connect to revenue and customer value, and you contribute directly alongside the team, through the same review and planning process as everyone else.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scalable, high-performance web products, CI/CD, DevOps, and security principles. SEO or search-related experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills. Comfortable presenting to boards, working with executives, and collaborating cross-functionally. Communication is async-first in our remote environment, leaning on clear, timely updates with documentation up-to-date and readable and proactive context-sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What’s in it for You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ultimate flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re 100% remote. Work from wherever you like, whenever you like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Freedom and autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; High-trust environment with lots of independence to solve problems your way, with support when you need it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum bureaucracy:&lt;/strong&gt; We stay efficient and keep momentum sustainable. No death by meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real impact:&lt;/strong&gt; This is a C-level role with a seat at the executive table, board visibility, and the mandate to transform how we build product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Small &amp;amp; friendly team:&lt;/strong&gt; We help each other out, have fun, and don&#39;t take ourselves too seriously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our network:&lt;/strong&gt; Access to a community of SaaS professionals across the&lt;a href=&quot;http://saas.group&quot;&gt; saas.group&lt;/a&gt; portfolio who regularly exchange ideas and expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible time off:&lt;/strong&gt; Recharge when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Budget:&lt;/strong&gt; Generous budget for classes, conferences, books, and other learning resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prerender is part of&lt;a href=&quot;http://saas.group/&quot;&gt; saas.group&lt;/a&gt;, and we have a shared goal of succeeding together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What is saas.group?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think of us as the driving catalyst behind your favorite software success stories. saas.group, established in 2017, is on a mission to turbocharge promising B2B SaaS ventures, unlocking their full potential. As a Software-as-a-Service portfolio powerhouse, we specialize in acquiring small software treasures and polishing them into industry stars. With a dynamic, fully remote team of nearly 380+ colleagues spanning 50+ countries we are truly global and we are rewriting the playbook on SaaS innovation and collaboration. We grow &lt;a href=&quot;https://saas.group/family/&quot;&gt;25 exciting brands&lt;/a&gt; under our umbrella. Feel free to explore our &lt;a href=&quot;https://saas.group/candidate-hub/&quot;&gt;Candidate&#39;s Hub&lt;/a&gt; to get an insider&#39;s view, dive into our culture, gain valuable insights into our teams and how we work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, don’t forget to follow &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/saas-group/&quot;&gt;saas.group on LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; to stay up-to-date on our job openings, podcast episodes, and with all things happening at our company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don’t just simply offer you to “take a job with us” but rather to “join us on this journey” to build the world&#39;s largest platform of independent SaaS companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sounds like something you’re up for? Feel free to apply even if you don’t check all these boxes. We believe in the power of diversity and fresh perspectives to spice up our team. Your application might just be the missing ingredient!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;—&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;saas.group is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. If you&#39;re passionate about working with a team that values innovation, excellence, and fairness, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We believe in fair and transparent pay. Salary ranges at saas.group are location-adjusted, targeting local market medians for a remote-first environment, and will be shared with our potential future employees in writing before your first interview - so you have everything you need to evaluate the opportunity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This role is part of our Central Marketing Team at saas.group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What is saas.group?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think of us as the driving catalyst behind your favorite software success stories. saas.group, established in 2017, is on a mission to turbocharge promising B2B SaaS ventures, unlocking their full potential. As a Software-as-a-Service portfolio powerhouse, we specialize in acquiring small software treasures and polishing them into industry stars. With a dynamic, fully remote team of nearly 400 colleagues spanning 50+ countries we are truly global and we are rewriting the playbook on SaaS innovation and collaboration. We grow &lt;a href=&quot;https://saas.group/family/&quot;&gt;25 exciting brands&lt;/a&gt; under our umbrella. Feel free to explore our &lt;a href=&quot;https://saas.group/candidate-hub/&quot;&gt;Candidate&#39;s Hub&lt;/a&gt; to get an insider&#39;s view, dive into our culture, gain valuable insights into our teams and how we work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, don&#39;t forget to follow&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/saas-group/&quot;&gt;saas.group on LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt; to stay up-to-date on our job openings, podcast episodes, and with all things happening at our company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Profile Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At saas.group paid acquisition across our portfolio runs through a small network of experienced PPC freelancers. We&#39;re looking for a German-speaking Performance Marketing Lead to oversee this: someone who owns the standards, strategy and quality bar for paid across our portfolio, from accounts ranging from small to large monthly budgets. The role goes beyond people-management, with continued hands-on responsibilities. You&#39;ll set the systems and direction and lead the freelancer network, but you&#39;ll also be in the accounts yourself on the most valuable brands, and you&#39;ll be the person we trust to judge whether the work being done is actually good. If you want real ownership of a function where your work impacts 25+ brands, this is that role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your immediate impact in the first 3-6 months will be:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of our most valuable paid accounts and demonstrably move performance, while keeping smaller-budget accounts efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a consistent standard across all brand accounts: how campaigns are structured, how conversions are tracked, how performance is reported, so there&#39;s a consistent quality bar across the whole portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take over the paid accounts of a newly acquired brand cleanly: audit, tracking check and handover with no performance dip.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own paid performance strategy and standards across the portfolio, and run the most valuable accounts hands-on yourself (Google Ads, Microsoft Ads, LinkedIn, and others), including ad copy and landing page testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support our PPC freelancers: set targets, review accounts, approve budgets, run regular syncs, challenge the &quot;why&quot; behind decisions, and keep the rest of marketing in the loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise brands directly on strategy and budget allocation, with the ability to push back, manage expectations and tell a brand honestly when a channel or budget won&#39;t deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take over newly acquired brands&#39; paid setups and build the systems, documentation and reporting that let performance scale across more brands and freelancers without losing the quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with our data analytics team on tracking, attribution and the flow of CRM data back into the ad platforms, and support the M&amp;amp;A team on due diligence for paid-heavy acquisition targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly connect with the SEO Team Lead to remain aligned with campaigns and strategies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring to the table&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years owning paid budgets (think €1M+ a year) while staying genuinely hands-on: you can open an account, diagnose it and run the full campaign yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated B2B lead-gen experience on search: comfortable with low conversion volumes, long sales cycles and optimising for lead quality over click counts (B2B SaaS, B2B or adjacent backgrounds such as gaming portfolios are welcome, as long as you can translate them to B2B).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record across very different budget sizes, from a few thousand a month to six figures a month, making small budgets work through sharp targeting and prioritisation rather than leaning on automated bidding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Google Ads and Microsoft Ads expertise, strong LinkedIn Ads experience, and the curiosity to pick up new platforms as brands need them. You&#39;re also confident with the measurement stack behind paid: GA4, Google Tag Manager, offline conversion imports and CRM integration. Experience with ChatGPT ads is a bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German at C1 or native: strong enough to write compelling German ad copy, alongside fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine AI fluency, and the drive to put it to work. You already use AI tools (Claude especially) in your day-to-day, and you&#39;re the kind of person who looks for where they can sharpen paid performance, from research and analysis to campaign and reporting workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s in it for you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ultimate flexibility: We&#39;re 100% remote. You can work from wherever you like, whenever you like.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Freedom and autonomy: We&#39;re a high-trust team, and you&#39;ll be given lots of flexibility to solve problems in your own way - with plenty of help from the team when you need it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum bureaucracy: We don&#39;t like to get bogged down with meetings and red tape. We like to be efficient and keep momentum steady &amp;amp; sustainable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Small &amp;amp; friendly team: We help each other out, have fun, and joke around.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our network: We are a community of entrepreneurial SaaS professionals that regularly exchange ideas, knowledge, learning and expertise with each other internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible time off: We want you to recharge your batteries when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t just simply offer you to &quot;take a job with us&quot; but rather to &quot;join us on this journey&quot; to build the world&#39;s largest platform of independent SaaS companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sounds like something you&#39;re up for? Feel free to apply even if you don&#39;t check all these boxes. We believe in the power of diversity and fresh perspectives to spice up our team. Your application might just be the missing ingredient!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;—&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;saas.group is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. If you&#39;re passionate about working with a team that values innovation, excellence, and fairness, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We believe in fair and transparent pay. Salary ranges at saas.group are location-adjusted, targeting local market medians for a remote-first environment, and will be shared with our potential future employees in writing before your first interview - so you have everything you need to evaluate the opportunity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Diese Position ist Teil unseres Central Leadership Teams bei &lt;a href=&quot;https://saas.group&quot;&gt; saas.group.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Was ist saas.group?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0&quot;&gt;Stell dir uns als den Beschleuniger hinter deinen Lieblings-Software-Erfolgsgeschichten vor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2&quot;&gt;. Die saas.group wurde 2017 gegründet und hat es sich zur Aufgabe gemacht, vielversprechende B2B-SaaS-Unternehmen auf das nächste Level zu heben und ihr volles Potenzial zu entfalten&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4&quot;&gt;. Als Software-as-a-Service-Portfolio-Powerhouse haben wir uns darauf spezialisiert, kleine Software-Schätze zu erwerben und sie zu Branchenstars zu entwickeln&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;3,6&quot;&gt;. Mit einem dynamischen, vollständig remote arbeitenden Team von fast 350+ Kolleginnen und Kollegen in über 50 Ländern sind wir global aufgestellt und schreiben das Regelbuch für SaaS-Innovation und Zusammenarbeit neu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;3,8&quot;&gt;. Unter unserem Dach führen wir mittlerweile 21 spannende Marken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;3,10&quot;&gt;. Wirf gerne einen Blick in unseren Candidate&#39;s Hub, um einen Einblick in unsere Kultur, unsere Teams und unsere Arbeitsweise zu erhalten&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;3,12&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;4,0&quot;&gt;Folge der saas.group auch auf LinkedIn, um über aktuelle Stellenangebote, Podcast-Folgen und Neuigkeiten aus unserem Unternehmen auf dem Laufenden zu bleiben&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;4,2&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Profil-Überblick&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_1c795b13c79aa7b0-33&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,0&quot;&gt;Wir suchen eine präsente, durchsetzungsstarke und detailorientierte Persönlichkeit als Geschäftsführer (m/w/d) für die SaaS.group GmbH, unsere deutsche Konzerngesellschaft mit Sitz in Schönefeld&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,2&quot;&gt;. In dieser Rolle übernahmst du als eingetragene:r Geschäftsführer:in vor Ort die operative Verantwortung und übst echte Entscheidungsbefugnisse aus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,4&quot;&gt;. Du steuerst die Büroorganisation sowie die laufende Buchhaltung und hältst Finanzen und Verwaltung zuverlässig auf Kurs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,6&quot;&gt;. Du bist das Gesicht der Gesellschaft vor Ort für Behörden, Finanzämter, Banken, Wirtschaftsprüfer und externe Dienstleister und arbeitest gleichzeitig eng mit unseren zentralen Legal-, Accounting- und Finanz-Teams zusammen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;6,8&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_1c795b13c79aa7b0-34&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;7,0&quot;&gt;Diese Rolle bietet eine einzigartige Chance für erfahrene Profis aus dem Finanz- oder Office-Management-Bereich in der Region Berlin/Brandenburg, die den nächsten Karriereschritt in eine offizielle Organ- und Führungsfunktion innerhalb einer internationalen, schnell wachsenden Software-Gruppe machen möchten&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;7,2&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Dein Beitrag in den ersten 3–6 Monaten:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li id=&quot;p-rc_1c795b13c79aa7b0-35&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0&quot;&gt;Nahtlose Übernahme der Position als eingetragene:r Geschäftsführer:in der SaaS.group GmbH sowie Etablierung effektiver organisatorischer Abläufe im Büro Schönefeld&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,2&quot;&gt;Übernahme der vollständigen Überwachung der lokalen Buchhaltung (Kreditoren, Debitoren, Belegwesen) und Optimierung der Vorbereitung von Monatsabschlüssen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,4&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,4&quot;&gt;Aufbau enger Arbeitsbeziehungen zu unseren externen Steuerberatern, Wirtschaftsprüfern, Banken sowie zu unseren internen Group-Accounting- und Legal-Teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,6&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,6&quot;&gt;Sicherstellung der vollen Einhaltung aller gesellschaftsrechtlichen Pflichten, Handelsregisterangelegenheiten und internen Geschäftsordnungen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;9,8&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Deine Aufgaben&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,0&quot;&gt;Lokale Geschäftsführung der SaaS.group GmbH am Standort Schönefeld mit voller Verantwortung für Freigaben, Vertragszeichnungen und Zahlungsverkehr im Rahmen der festgelegten Geschäftsordnung&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,2&quot;&gt;Eigenverantwortliche Durchführung und Steuerung der laufenden Buchhaltung (Kreditoren, Debitoren, Belegmanagement) sowie Vorbereitung der Monats- und Jahresabschlüsse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,4&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,4&quot;&gt;Enge Zusammenarbeit mit Steuerberatern und Wirtschaftsprüfern bei Umsatzsteuer-Voranmeldungen, Jahresabschlüssen und Prüfungen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,6&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,6&quot;&gt;Erfüllung aller gesellschaftsrechtlichen Vorgaben nach deutschem Recht (u. a. Pflege des Transparenzregisters, Vorbereitung von Gesellschafterbeschlüssen und Handelsregisteranmeldungen)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,8&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,8&quot;&gt;Verantwortung für das Office-Management vor Ort in Schönefeld (Postbearbeitung, Dienstleisterverträge, Büroorganisation sowie Archivierung)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,10&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,10&quot;&gt;Zentrale Ansprechperson vor Ort für das Finanzamt, Banken, Behörden und Versicherer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;11,12&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Das bringst Du mit&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0&quot;&gt;Eine erfolgreich abgeschlossene kaufmännische Ausbildung (z. B. Steuerfachangestellte:r, Bilanzbuchhalter:in, Kaufleute für Büromanagement) oder eine vergleichbare Qualifikation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,2&quot;&gt;Mehrjährige praktische Erfahrung in der Buchhaltung, Finanzadministration oder im leitenden Office-Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,4&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,4&quot;&gt;Fundierte Kenntnisse im Umgang mit DATEV (oder vergleichbarer Buchhaltungssoftware) sowie modernen digitalen Werkzeugen (MS Office / Google Workspace)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,6&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,6&quot;&gt;Verhandlungssichere Deutschkenntnisse sowie gute Englischkenntnisse für die reibungslose Zusammenarbeit in unserer internationalen Unternehmensgruppe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,8&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,8&quot;&gt;Bereitschaft, rechtliche Verantwortung und Haftung als eingetragene:r Geschäftsführer:in zu übernehmen (Führungserfahrung ist ein Plus, aber keine Voraussetzung)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,10&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,10&quot;&gt;Wohnsitz in der Region Berlin/Brandenburg sowie die Bereitschaft zur regelmäßigen physischen Präsenz im Büro in Schönefeld&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;13,12&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Was wir Dir bieten&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;15,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Echte Verantwortung:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Eine vollwertige Geschäftsführungsposition mit klarer Geschäftsordnung, Absicherung durch eine D&amp;amp;O-Versicherung und direkter Zusammenarbeit mit dem Group CFO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-path-to-node=&quot;15,2&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
